' BRAIN GAMES II
' Five more puzzles from the "Brain Games" chapter of Tim Hartnell's
' Giant Book of Computer Games (Ballantine Books, 1984; Interface
' Publications, 1983), for the ColecoVision in Amy by Amy Bienvenu.
'
' MUMBLE MARBLE: solitaire. Jump a marble over its neighbour into an
' empty hole; the jumped marble is taken. End with one marble, in the
' centre.
' CYCLOTRON: three particles of antimatter hide in seven tubes. Fire atoms
' in and see where they come out: antimatter absorbs an atom (one time in
' ten) or knocks it into the next tube. Six seconds (goes) to say where
' the antimatter is.
' SWITCHEROO: the digits 1 to 9, mixed. Pick a place: every digit from
' there to the end is turned round. Put them in order.
' FLIPPER: nine discs, stars and Xs. Hit a star: it becomes an X and its
' neighbours turn over. Leave one X, in the middle.
' SEARCHING FOR DARYL: find Daryl in cave 29 of a maze of tunnels, then
' bring him back to cave 1. The compass and the proximeter help.
'
' Controls (either joystick): the stick moves the pointer, the button
' acts; in MUMBLE MARBLE the button picks a marble, then its hole (the
' second button drops it). The second button leaves. Keypad not used.
'
' Liberties taken:
' - MUMBLE MARBLE: the listing lets any marble move to any hole and only
'   counts the marbles of the first row; here only real jumps are
'   allowed, all marbles are counted, and the game ends when no jump is
'   left (won with one marble in the centre).
' - CYCLOTRON: the listing's deflection (INT(RND*2)-1) can only push an
'   atom to the left; here it goes left or right, one chance in two. The
'   atom is seen flying; a hit is shown as a bounce.
' - FLIPPER: a start with no star (no move possible) or already solved is
'   dealt again. As in the listing, hitting an X does nothing but counts.
' - SEARCHING FOR DARYL: the tunnels are chosen with the stick; the moves
'   are counted; the proximeter is also drawn as a bar.
' - New pictures (the board, the cyclotron, the number blocks, the discs,
'   the caves, the explorer and Daryl), new music (Deep Thought), sounds.
'
' House rules kept: text in columns 2-29 and rows 1-22; at most two
' sprites; every screen is drawn with the NMI off after a wait.

const TMarble00 = 128
const TMarble01 = 129
const TMarble10 = 130
